**Setup & run:**
```bash
npm install
npm start
```

**API endpoints:**

**POST /signup** — Register user
```json
{"email": "user@example.com", "password": "securepass123"}
```
Returns: `{userId, email}`

**POST /login** — Authenticate and get session
```json
{"email": "user@example.com", "password": "securepass123"}
```
Returns: `{sessionToken, userId, email}`

**POST /logout** — Invalidate session
```json
{"sessionToken": "..."}
```

**GET /me** — Verify session (send token in `Authorization: Bearer <token>` header)
Returns: `{id, email, createdAt}`

**Security features:**
- bcrypt hashing (10 rounds) on password storage
- Rate limiting: 5 failed attempts per 15 minutes per email → 429 response
- UUID sessions in-memory, cleared on logout
- DB constraints prevent duplicate emails
- 8-char minimum password length
